h('ABSTRACT');p('YojanaMitra is a web application that helps students discover scholarships, public opportunities, jobs, and internships; understand recorded eligibility conditions; and organize applications. A student account stores a profile with details such as course, category, annual family income, domicile, marks, and language. The server compares that profile with structured scheme rules and returns a status with reasons. Missing inputs and extra manual conditions remain “Maybe” instead of being treated as a pass.')
p('The system uses a React and TypeScript client built with Vite, an Express and TypeScript API, Prisma ORM, and SQLite. Authenticated records include profile, bookmarks, applications, document checklist entries, and assistant sessions. The app has opportunity discovery, job tracking, administrator review, and an assistant with separate YojanaMitra and general modes. Optional voice input and speech output depend on browser capability, microphone permission, and configured transcription providers.')
p('The report explains the system with architecture, data-flow, database, user-flow, and eligibility diagrams and includes screenshots from the local application. At the evaluation run, nine server tests passed; server/client TypeScript checks and production builds completed. These results confirm code paths exercised by the checks, not the accuracy of every seeded scheme or the availability of external AI providers. The official portal remains the authority for current eligibility, documents, benefits, and deadlines.');p('Keywords: student support, scholarships, eligibility, application tracking, conversational assistant, React, Express, SQLite.');br()
