# Chapter 1
begin_chapter_section();h('CHAPTER 1  INTRODUCTION');h('1.1 Background',2)
p('Students often find scholarships, education support, internships, and recruitment notices across separate portals. Each opportunity can have different eligibility conditions, document lists, dates, and application steps. A student must compare these requirements with personal details, prepare certificates, and remember multiple application statuses. Scattered information increases the chance of overlooking a suitable opportunity or relying on an old summary.')
p('YojanaMitra organizes discovery and preparation in one authenticated workspace. Students save a profile, search a catalog, compare their details with recorded rules, save opportunities, track applications, and open official sources. An assistant answers questions using relevant stored records in its guidance mode, while a separate general mode does not receive profile or catalog context.')
h('1.2 Problem statement',2);p('The project addresses the repetitive work of finding opportunities and managing application preparation. Students need an accessible way to compare stated rules with their profile, understand what remains unknown, retain their details between visits, and track next steps. The system must not turn incomplete or unreviewed information into a promise of eligibility or an official deadline.')
h('1.3 Aim and objectives',2);table(['Objective','Project support'],[('Discovery','Search scholarships, government/private jobs, and internships.'),('Personal comparison','Apply explicit rule checks and explain outcomes.'),('Persistence','Save profile, bookmarks, documents, applications, and chat sessions per account.'),('Preparation','Provide checklists, source links, and a student-managed tracker.'),('Conversational support','Provide grounded guidance and separate general chat, with optional voice.'),('Review','Track sources and require administrator verification for publication.')],9)
h('1.4 Scope and boundaries',2);p('Implemented functions include accounts, profiles, opportunity search, rule-based screening, bookmarks, scheme/job application tracking, document checklist, chat history, voice controls, and administrator review. The app does not submit forms to external portals, issue certificates, verify identity with a government system, guarantee awards, or replace an official notification. External AI depends on provider configuration, quota, network, and model availability. Stored opportunity data requires human review for the active cycle.')
h('1.5 Intended users',2);table(['Actor','Tasks'],[('Student','Maintain profile, discover and compare records, prepare documents, track applications, ask questions.'),('Administrator','Review scheme sources/rules, knowledge excerpts, and draft job notices.'),('Official portal','Authoritative source for current eligibility, documents, dates, and application instructions.')],9)
h('1.6 Report organization',2);p('Chapter 2 reviews information sources, manual workflows, rule-based screening, assistants, and the project technology. Chapter 3 explains requirements, architecture, data flows, schema, interface, processing, and security. Chapter 4 reports tests and their limits. Chapter 5 concludes and lists practical improvements.')

# Chapter 2
br();h('CHAPTER 2  LITERATURE SURVEY');h('2.1 Opportunity information sources',2)
p('Scholarship and recruitment details are published by government departments, institutions, examinations, and recruiting organizations. Their official portals and notices are authoritative for eligibility, documents, benefit, and deadlines. An aggregator can improve navigation, but it should preserve a source link and should not present a summary as a replacement for the publishing authority.')
p('Students may also encounter private aggregators, social posts, coaching pages, and forwarded messages. These can help surface an opportunity but may be incomplete or stale. YojanaMitra records source URLs, review state, and dates and asks users to verify current details on the official portal. Deadlines and rules can change each cycle.')
h('2.2 Manual workflow limitations',2);p('A manual process asks students to search each portal, maintain a calendar, save documents separately, and remember whether an application is planned, submitted, or under review. It is possible but repetitive. Comparing income ceilings, course types, domicile, marks, and category across notices also takes attention.')
p('The project consolidates these activities. A saved profile reduces repeated entry; an explainable comparison surfaces known matches and missing data; bookmarks preserve options; and the tracker stores status and notes. These are organization tools. A public authority still decides the final application outcome.')
h('2.3 Rule-based screening',2);p('A deterministic engine compares explicit fields in structured data. It can test annual income against a threshold, category against an allowed list, or marks against a minimum and give a reason for each result. Its trustworthiness depends on accurate profile values and source rules, and it cannot infer conditions that have not been modeled.')
p('YojanaMitra reports “Not eligible” when a modeled requirement fails, “Maybe” when required data is missing or a manual condition remains, and “Eligible” only when the modeled conditions pass. Empty rule sets do not produce a positive result. Even a pass includes a reminder to check the official portal.')
h('2.4 Conversational assistants and retrieval',2);p('A conversational assistant accepts ordinary-language questions. In grounded mode, the server retrieves relevant scheme, job, or knowledge records and supplies that context to a configured model. Source links can accompany the reply. The model instructions discourage invented dates and eligibility rules. When providers fail, the system can show stored guidance or an offline response.')
p('General mode deliberately omits profile information and retrieved scheme data. Voice support uses browser speech functions where available or a configured transcription provider for recorded audio. Provider quota, model availability, browser implementation, and microphone permissions affect results. The assistant remains guidance, not an official decision.')
h('2.5 Technology comparison',2);table(['Technology','Role','Project fit'],[('React 19','Interactive client components','Reusable stateful interface.'),('TypeScript 5','Static typing','Checks API and rule data shapes.'),('Vite 7','Development and bundling','Client development and production build.'),('Node.js / Express 5','HTTP API','Middleware and application routes.'),('Prisma 6 / SQLite','Database access','Typed model access with compact relational persistence.'),('Zod','Runtime validation','Rejects invalid requests at server boundaries.')],8)
h('2.6 Security and privacy principles',2);p('The implementation uses authentication, Argon2 password hashing, per-user queries, Zod validation, CSRF checks for mutations, Helmet security headers, and rate limits for login and AI chat. Authentication uses an HTTP-only cookie. The API sends no-store headers outside tests. Guidance mode passes a limited masked profile summary; general mode receives no profile or local scheme context. Account export and deletion routes are implemented.')
p('These controls reduce common risks but are not an independent penetration test. A deployment still needs a strong secret, HTTPS, correct allowed origins, database backup and restore, careful provider-key handling, dependency updates, and a human source-review process.')
h('2.7 Summary',2);p('The design combines discovery and personal task management while preserving source links and uncertainty. Rule checks provide transparent reasons; the assistant helps with natural-language questions. Ongoing human data review remains essential because code validation cannot prove that a transcribed official rule is correct.')

# Chapter 3
br();h('CHAPTER 3  SYSTEM DEVELOPMENT');h('3.1 Development structure',2);p('The system is separated into a browser client, an API, shared route constants, and a database. The browser gathers input and displays status; the server validates requests and applies security/business rules; Prisma persists data in SQLite. Sensitive account access and eligibility evaluation occur server-side rather than relying on transient page state.')
h('3.2 Functional requirements',2);table(['ID','Requirement','Expected behaviour'],[('FR1','Account','Register, sign in, inspect session, sign out.'),('FR2','Profile','Save student data and retrieve it after refresh/sign-in.'),('FR3','Discovery','Search opportunities and show source, review notice, deadline, and match reasons.'),('FR4','Eligibility','Return three-state status with reasons from structured criteria.'),('FR5','Tracking','Manage bookmarks, application statuses, and notes.'),('FR6','Documents','Maintain checklist items and direct users to authoritative instructions.'),('FR7','Jobs','View published notices and track/bookmark job applications.'),('FR8','Assistant','Choose grounded or general mode and retain user-owned chat sessions.'),('FR9','Voice','Accept speech and optionally speak replies where supported.'),('FR10','Administration','Edit scheme/knowledge data and review/publish job notices.'),('FR11','Data rights','Export account records or delete account after password confirmation.')],8)
h('3.3 Quality requirements',2);table(['Area','Design / evidence'],[('Usability','Workspace navigation, form labels, status explanations, EN/HI/MR language labels.'),('Reliability','Database persistence, request validation, missing data remains uncertain.'),('Security','Argon2, signed session cookie, CSRF, Helmet, rate limits, scoped queries.'),('Privacy','General AI mode omits profile and retrieval context; guidance sends limited masked summary.'),('Maintainability','Separate workspaces, shared route constants, Prisma schema, deterministic tested logic.'),('Accessibility','Semantic controls/labels/live regions exist; a full assistive-technology audit remains future work.'),('Portability','Client/server can run independently and be built for deployment.')],8)
h('3.4 System architecture',2);p('Figure 3.1 shows the browser, React client, Express API, SQLite database, and optional AI providers. Requests pass through server authentication and validation. Prisma reads or writes application data. AI requests reach a configured external or local provider; browser speech facilities support optional input/output.');picture('arch','Figure 3.1  Client, API, database, and AI provider architecture')
h('3.5 Data-flow diagrams',2);h('3.5.1 Level 0 context',3);p('Figure 3.2 treats the application as one process. Students provide profile details, questions, and status updates; administrators provide reviewed records. The system returns matches, explanations, and tracker information. Official portals remain outside the system boundary and provide final confirmation.');picture('d0','Figure 3.2  DFD Level 0: actors and system boundary')
h('3.5.2 Level 1 processes',3);p('Figure 3.3 separates profile/account, catalog, eligibility, tracking, assistant, and administration. These processes use the persistent store, while private records are scoped to the signed-in account. A student may progress from profile and search to eligibility and then save or track an opportunity.');picture('d1','Figure 3.3  DFD Level 1: main processes and data store',5.9)
h('3.5.3 Level 2 eligibility',3);p('Figure 3.4 expands eligibility calculation. The system combines a profile with a scheme’s rules, checks supported criteria, and keeps missing values unknown. A failed requirement produces Not eligible; missing information or an unmodeled condition produces Maybe; a complete pass produces Eligible with reasons and a reminder.');picture('d2','Figure 3.4  DFD Level 2: profile-to-result flow')
h('3.6 User journeys',2);p('Figure 3.5 shows student and administrator actions. Students search and inspect records, manage their profile and application work, and ask questions. Administrators review source-linked content. A student must open the current notice and submit applications independently.');picture('use','Figure 3.5  Student and administrator use cases')
h('3.7 Database model',2);p('User is the root account entity. Profile is optional and has a unique userId. Scheme and JobPost contain different kinds of opportunities. Application, Bookmark, JobApplication, and JobBookmark link accounts to opportunities with uniqueness constraints that prevent duplicate tracking. ChatSession belongs to a user and contains messages with source references. Account deletion cascades through dependent data.')
picture('er','Figure 3.6  Simplified entity relationship model',5.9);table(['Entity','Purpose / key fields'],[('User','Account email, role, password hash.'),('Profile','Category, income, location/domicile, course, marks, language.'),('Scheme','Rules, benefits, documents, deadline, source, verification dates.'),('Application / Bookmark','User-to-scheme tracking and saved opportunity.'),('JobPost','Notice, qualifications, dates, source evidence, review state.'),('ChatSession / Message','Owner, title, text, role, sources, timestamps.'),('KnowledgeChunk','Topic, language, source URL/name, review state.'),('JobApplication / JobBookmark','User-to-job tracking and saved opportunity.')],8)
h('3.8 API design',2);p('Express routes group authentication, profile, schemes, bookmarks, applications, documents, jobs, chat sessions, AI, and administration. Shared route constants reduce client/server path mismatch. Authentication middleware reads the session cookie. Mutations compare a CSRF header with a cookie. Administrator routes require ADMIN role. Zod validates input before database writes.')
h('3.9 Eligibility engine',2);p('The TypeScript engine supports income ceilings/floors, category, course keywords, course type, minimum marks, state, gender, domicile, disability, age range, and manual checks. Missing required values create reasons. A failed check yields Not eligible; uncertainty yields Maybe; and only complete modeled success yields Eligible. The job evaluator uses the notification cutoff date and recorded category relaxation, while incomplete age or qualification data remains uncertain.')
picture('elig','Figure 3.7  Decision logic for the eligibility outcomes')
p('For an income ceiling, an amount equal to the limit passes the criterion; one rupee above fails it. Missing income is not treated as zero. Manual checks prevent a complete-pass result until the student checks the official condition. These behaviours are covered by automated server tests.')
h('3.10 Assistant and voice flow',2);p('Figure 3.8 shows typed or spoken input, the chat API, mode-specific context, and reply. Guidance mode retrieves relevant local records and a limited profile summary. General mode skips profile and catalog retrieval. The server stores sessions and source references. If providers are unavailable, it returns stored guidance where possible or an explicit offline response.')
picture('ai','Figure 3.8  Assistant request path and optional voice processing')
p('Voice input uses browser speech recognition when available; otherwise the client can record audio for server-side transcription through configured providers. Browser speech synthesis reads responses and supports speed, pause/resume, stop, and hands-free options. Permission or provider failure should leave typed input usable.')
h('3.11 User interface',2);p('The workspace navigation includes overview, schemes, jobs, applications, profile, documents, and AI assistant. Opportunity cards show benefits text, a deadline value, last-verified state, eligibility result and reason, official source, and actions. “Check official site” and review notices distinguish unverified catalog data from official confirmation.')
p('Screenshot 3.9 shows the profile form. Saving calls the authenticated profile endpoint, which stores the values in the database. On browser refresh the app requests the profile again from the server, so data persists while the account remains signed in; it is not only held in React memory.')
x=doc.add_paragraph();x.alignment=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER;x.add_run().add_picture(str(shot_profile),width=Inches(6.0));p('Screenshot 3.9  Student profile page captured from the local YojanaMitra app.',True,True)
p('Screenshot 3.10 shows assistant mode selection, conversation history, message area, microphone input, reply speech controls, speed, and voice conversation. The page presents a reminder to verify guidance on the official portal and avoid entering sensitive identity or banking information.')
x=doc.add_paragraph();x.alignment=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER;x.add_run().add_picture(str(shot_ai),width=Inches(6.0));p('Screenshot 3.10  AI assistant screen captured from the local YojanaMitra app.',True,True)
h('3.12 Source verification and administration',2);p('Scheme records store structured rules/documents, official and source URLs, verification state/date, and a notice. Changing source or rule content clears prior verification. Server checks require an exact verification status, real date, complete non-placeholder fields, a specific official page, and no unresolved conflict in the notes. This prevents accidental verification but cannot judge whether a person copied a rule accurately.')
p('Job records store the official notification, source details, qualifications, age rules, fees, dates, documents, and selection process. New jobs begin as drafts. Publishing requires an official notification URL and administrator verification. Stale non-evergreen published notices can be moved back to draft for review.')
h('3.13 Security and privacy',2);table(['Control','Implementation','Purpose'],[('Passwords','Argon2 hash; strong password validation.','Avoid storing raw password.'),('Session','Signed JWT in HTTP-only cookie; seven-day expiry; SameSite=Lax.','Keep session token out of browser scripts.'),('CSRF','Random cookie/header equality on mutations.','Protect state-changing routes.'),('Validation','Zod schemas and JSON/audio limits.','Reject invalid or oversized inputs.'),('Access scope','User identity used in private record queries.','Limit data to account owner.'),('Browser protections','Helmet, microphone policy, API no-store headers.','Reduce common exposure.'),('Rate limits','Login/AI limits and failed-login tracking.','Slow guessing and overuse.'),('AI minimization','General mode gets no profile; guidance sends a limited masked summary.','Reduce provider data exposure.')],7)
h('3.14 Design trade-offs',2);p('SQLite simplifies local setup and is appropriate for an academic demonstration. A public multi-user deployment may require a managed database and tested backups. Deterministic rules are explainable but cannot capture every exception in a long notification. AI accepts natural questions but varies with provider behaviour and is therefore not used as the eligibility authority.')

# Chapter 4
br();h('CHAPTER 4  PERFORMANCE EVALUATION');h('4.1 Evaluation method',2);p('Evaluation used automated server tests, project-wide TypeScript checks, and production builds. These checks assess internal code behaviour and buildability. They do not constitute a large-scale load benchmark, external security certification, or factual review of all opportunity records.')
h('4.2 Environment and commands',2);p('Checks were run in the project workspace on 16 October 2026 with installed Node.js/npm dependencies. Commands were `npm test -w server`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`. The test command runs Node tests through tsx; typechecking covers server and client; the build compiles the server and creates the client Vite bundle.')
h('4.3 Results',2);table(['Check','Observed outcome','Interpretation'],[('Server tests','9 passed; 0 failed.','Covered eligibility, jobs, search normalization, and tracker verification.'),('Typecheck','Completed for server and client.','No TypeScript errors reported in this run.'),('Production build','Server compilation and client Vite build completed.','Both workspaces built locally.'),('Screenshots','Profile and assistant screens captured.','Documents the UI; not a cross-browser usability audit.')],8)
h('4.4 Boundary cases',2);table(['Scenario','Expected behavior','Reason'],[('Income equals ceiling','Criterion passes.','Exact boundary is inclusive.'),('Income one rupee over','Criterion fails.','Ceiling is enforced.'),('Required profile value missing','Maybe with reason.','Unknown is not a pass.'),('Empty/unverified rule object','Maybe, with portal reminder.','Blank rule data cannot assert eligibility.'),('Manual official condition remains','Maybe.','Unmodeled exception remains unresolved.'),('Job age with cutoff/relaxation','Calculate using notice cutoff and category value.','Uses date stated by recruiting authority.')],8)
h('4.5 Test coverage and gaps',2);table(['Area','Current automated coverage / gap'],[('Eligibility','Unverified rules, income boundary, manual criteria.'),('Jobs','Common job-question recognition and cutoff-based age relaxations.'),('Search','Normalization of common scholarship queries.'),('Tracker verification','Exact Yes, real date, complete data, specific source, conflict notes.'),('Not in nine server tests','Browser end-to-end, microphone permissions, external provider availability, penetration tests, load, factual audit of seeded records.')],8)
h('4.6 Functional walkthrough',2);p('A student can register, sign in, complete and save a profile, search opportunities, inspect a source and eligibility explanation, bookmark or track a record, manage document notes, and ask the assistant. The assistant selector permits choosing general mode separately. Voice tests require microphone permission and compatible browser support; typed input remains the fallback.')
h('4.7 Security review',2);p('Source inspection confirms authentication middleware, administrator role checks, password hashing, CSRF comparison for mutations, request validation, browser security headers, rate limits, and user-scoped queries. General mode skips profile and catalog context. These code-level controls have not been independently penetration-tested; production secret management, HTTPS, backups, and access operations still require attention.')
h('4.8 Performance interpretation',2);p('No response-time or concurrency benchmark is claimed. AI response time varies with provider latency, quota, network, and model availability. SQLite suits the local demonstration but needs evaluation before scaling. The uncertainty statuses and source notices are intentional because an unknown rule should not be presented as a confirmed answer.')
h('4.9 Limitations',2);table(['Limitation','Effect','Follow-up'],[('Seed accuracy not proven by code tests','Rules may be incomplete or stale.','Review each record on the current official page/GR.'),('Cycle dates change','Old deadline may be invalid.','Keep “Check official site” until confirmed.'),('AI provider dependency','Quota/network failure affects answers.','Monitor providers and keep offline/text fallback.'),('Browser voice variation','Microphone or recognition may fail.','Keep typed entry and clear status.'),('Not every clause is modeled','Exceptions require human review.','Use manual checks and Maybe.'),('No external load/security audit','Production readiness not established.','Test operations, security, accessibility, and scale before public launch.')],8)

# Chapter 5
br();h('CHAPTER 5  CONCLUSION AND FUTURE SCOPE');h('5.1 Conclusion',2);p('YojanaMitra brings opportunity discovery, profile-based screening, document preparation, application tracking, and conversational help into one web application. Its key design principle is to expose known conditions and missing information while keeping official portals as the final source. Three-state results communicate failures and incomplete checks rather than overstating certainty.')
p('The application has a React/TypeScript client, Express/TypeScript API, and Prisma/SQLite data layer. Account-associated data is persisted server-side. The project provides scheme and job workflows, reviewed-source mechanisms, separate grounded and general AI modes, and optional voice controls. In the recorded evaluation, nine server tests passed and project typechecking and builds completed.')
p('The implementation is suitable as an academic project and demonstration. Its usefulness depends on accurate current records and sound deployment operations. Automated checks verify only the conditions they exercise. Students should confirm current eligibility, documents, benefits, and application dates on official portals.')
h('5.2 Future enhancements',2);table(['Priority','Enhancement','Benefit'],[('1','Human source audit for every scheme/job.','Improves factual reliability and verified dates.'),('2','Review reminders and due/expired dashboard.','Makes maintenance repeatable.'),('3','Browser end-to-end and accessibility tests.','Covers real navigation, assistive technology, permissions.'),('4','Rule-type boundary tests.','Reduces regressions.'),('5','Production migrations and backup monitoring.','Improves deployed data resilience.'),('6','Consent-based saved-opportunity reminders.','Helps users follow deadlines.'),('7','Multilingual AI grounding/citation evaluation.','Measures quality in supported languages.'),('8','Realistic concurrency and managed database evaluation.','Creates scaling evidence.')],8)
h('5.3 Student reminder',2);p('Use YojanaMitra to organize discovery and preparation. Confirm eligibility, documents, benefit amount, dates, and instructions on the official portal. Never enter Aadhaar, PAN, bank details, or portal passwords into the assistant.')
